        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To evaluate a power, we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the resulting product.</p>",
            "readable_text": "To evaluate a power, we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the resulting product.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>So, to find the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9^2,]</span> we first write it out with multiplication signs as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "So, to find the value of [MATH: 9^2,] we first write it out with multiplication signs as follows:\n[MATH: 2]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Then, we compute the product:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9^{2} = 9 \u00d7 9 = 81]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Then, we compute the product:\n[MATH: 9^{2} = 9 \u00d7 9 = 81]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Raising a number to the power of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2]</span> is known as <strong>squaring</strong> a number. Therefore, the following are equivalent.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Raising a number to the power of [MATH: 2] is known as squaring a number. Therefore, the following are equivalent.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<ul><li><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9^2 = 81]</span></p></li><li><p>The <strong>square</strong> of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9]</span> is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 81.]</span> </p></li><li><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9]</span> raised to the <em>second</em> power equals <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 81.]</span> </p></li></ul>",
            "readable_text": "- [MATH: 9^2 = 81]\n- The square of [MATH: 9] is [MATH: 81.]\n- [MATH: 9] raised to the second power equals [MATH: 81.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nTo evaluate a power, we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the resulting product.\n\nContent:\nSo, to find the value of [MATH: 9^2,] we first write it out with multiplication signs as follows:\n[MATH: 2]\n\nContent:\nThen, we compute the product:\n[MATH: 9^{2} = 9 \u00d7 9 = 81]\n\nContent:\nRaising a number to the power of [MATH: 2] is known as squaring a number. Therefore, the following are equivalent.\n\nContent:\n- [MATH: 9^2 = 81]\n- The square of [MATH: 9] is [MATH: 81.]\n- [MATH: 9] raised to the second power equals [MATH: 81.]"
      },
